<p>NOTE: Fourth quarter earnings were hurt by a $13.3 million asset valuation charge in accordance with the Financial Accounting Standards Board's Statement 121.  &quot;Accounting for the impairment of Long-Lived Assets and for Long-Lived Assets to Be Disposed of&quot; (&quot;FAS 121&quot;).  Based upon a financial review of all 261 Company- owned restaurants operating at year-end, the FAS 121 charge applied to ten underperforming units.</p>
<p>Excluding the charge, net earnings would have been $8.6 million, or $0.17 per share.  Net earnings for the fourth quarter of 1995 amounted to $8.1 million, or $0.15 per share.</p>
<p>Fourth quarter of 1996 was a 13-week period while the fourth quarter of 1995 consisted of 14 weeks.</p>
<p>Similar to the fourth quarter, fiscal 1996 consisted of 52 weeks in comparison to fiscal 1995, which was a 53-week period. Net earnings for 1996 amounted to $28.6 million compared to $33.2 million in 1995, resulting in net earnings per share of $0.55 in 1996 and $0.62 in 1995.  Excluding the FAS 121 charge, net earnings for 1996 would have amounted to $37.0 million (up 11%), or $0.71 per share (up 15%).</p>
